WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.780
Chapter 1 separated an itch-producing input from the neurons carrying it.

2
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.900
Once those neurons fire, how can experiments order a spinal relay?

3
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.920
Carry the same teal pathway from skin into the dorsal horn.

4
00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:19.603
In one mouse model, the afferent supplies Nppb.

5
00:00:20.903 --> 00:00:25.163
Without Nppb, almost all tested itch responses disappeared.

6
00:00:26.603 --> 00:00:30.143
Injecting Nppb around the cord itself evoked scratching.

7
00:00:31.423 --> 00:00:35.683
The missing signal was upstream; downstream machinery could still respond.

8
00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:45.753
Next, researchers removed about 70 percent of spinal cells carrying NPRA, the Nppb

9
00:00:45.753 --> 00:00:51.633
receptor. If GRP acts later, should added GRP still evoke scratching?

10
00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.230
It still evoked scratching.

11
00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:08.450
The simplest order is sensory Nppb, then NPRA cells, GRP and GRPR.

12
00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:14.470
follow. A downstream signal bypassed loss of the proposed upstream population.

13
00:01:15.683 --> 00:01:19.403
Independent tests support the later GRPR step.

14
00:01:20.983 --> 00:01:25.023
Grpr-mutant mice scratched less to tested itch-producing agents.

15
00:01:26.303 --> 00:01:32.343
Removing GRPR-expressing spinal neurons also lowered scratching, while measured pain

16
00:01:32.343 --> 00:01:33.343
behaviours remained.

17
00:01:34.433 --> 00:01:37.213
This orders functions, not complete anatomy.

18
00:01:38.573 --> 00:01:40.893
The experiments did not show direct synapses.

19
00:01:42.253 --> 00:01:44.853
They did not identify one source of GRP.

20
00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:50.913
The sequence is one supported route in mice, not every itch route or a human

21
00:01:50.913 --> 00:01:51.913
circuit.

22
00:01:52.617 --> 00:01:54.617
Relays are only half the story.

23
00:01:56.377 --> 00:02:00.797
Bhlhb5-dependent spinal interneurons provide inhibition.

24
00:02:02.297 --> 00:02:05.977
Mice missing that developmental population scratched excessively.

25
00:02:07.457 --> 00:02:12.037
Removing a brake can raise output without strengthening the incoming itch-producing

26
00:02:12.037 --> 00:02:13.037
signal.

27
00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:16.267
Light touch can use another control route.

28
00:02:17.407 --> 00:02:23.027
Removing or silencing NPY-lineage spinal interneurons increased mechanical

29
00:02:23.027 --> 00:02:24.847
scratching in one paradigm.

30
00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:28.687
Tested chemical itch and pain did not rise.

31
00:02:30.047 --> 00:02:34.367
Mechanical scratching also survived GRPR-cell ablation there.

32
00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:37.170
Scratching can feed back too.

33
00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:42.910
In primate recordings, scratching suppressed histamine-evoked activity in

34
00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:44.190
spinothalamic neurons.

35
00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:48.550
It spared baseline and capsaicin-evoked activity.

36
00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.890
That is a firing measurement, not a reported sensation.

37
00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.460
The guiding rule now has its full circuit.

38
00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:02.200
Trigger, recruited population, spinal route, and inhibition together shape

39
00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:08.100
scratching. Use perturbations to order links, but do not mistake functional order

40
00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.120
for complete wiring.
